Synthesis of $(\mathbf{H}_{2}\mathbf{N}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{e}_{2})_{2}\mathbf{Fe}_{2}(\mathbf{Cl}_{2}\mathbf{dhbq})_{3}(\mathbf{D}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{F})_{0.4}$ (1). In a round bottom flask, a solution of chloranilic acid $(257\mathrm{mg})$ and dimethylamine $171~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of a $0.2{\bf M}$ aqueous solution) in $6~\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF was sparged with Ar for $15~\mathrm{min}$ . A separate, freshly prepared aqueous solution of 1 M $\mathrm{Fe}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{3}$ $(10~\mathrm{mL})$ was sparged with Ar for $15~\mathrm{min}$ . In air, $140~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of the $\mathrm{Fe}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{3}$ solution was quickly added to $1.4~\mathrm{mL}$ of the DMF solution in a thick-walled borosilicate tube. The reaction mixture was degassed with three freeze-pump-thaw cycles, and then the tube was flame-sealed and placed in an oven preheated to $120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . After $18\mathrm{h}$ , the tube was removed from the oven and allowed to cool to ambient temperature. The resulting black powder was filtered inside a Vacuum Atmospheres glovebox with a humid ${\bf N}_{2}$ atmosphere, and was then transferred to an MBraun glovebox with a dry Ar atmosphere. The crude product was soaked in $10\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF for $24\mathrm{h}$ , and then the supernatant was decanted and replaced with fresh DMF. This washing procedure was repeated two more times, and then the solid was filtered and rinsed with $1\ \mathrm{mL}$ of THF. The DMF-solvated material was then soaked in $10~\mathrm{mL}$ of THF at $50~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $48\ \mathrm{h}.$ , during which time the solvent was replaced with fresh THF three times. The material was then activated at $120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under reduced pressure to afford 1 as a black powder. Yield: $15~\mathrm{mg}$ $(26\%)$ . Anal. Calcd. for C23.2Cl6Fe2H18.8N2.4O12.4: C, 32.6; H, 2.2; N, 3.9. Found: C, 32.5; H, 2.3; N, 4.2. For spectroscopic and electrochemical experiments, many individual batches of the material were synthesized separately and combined for washing, activation, and characterization. IR (solid-ATR): 2786 (w), 1655 (s), 1478 (s), 1340 (s), 1251 (m), 1224 (m), 1190 (w), 1094 (m), 1060 (m), 1021 (m), 962 (w), 830 (w), 661 $\mathrm{{(m)}}$ , 488 (m) $\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ .
